    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for the Austin Waves is headlined by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (81.21) and **Jackson Merrill** (74.73), both of whom benefit from prime matchups against starters with subpar expected ERAs. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is our clear efficiency leader today; facing Jake Bennett (4.88 xERA) in a park providing a 7% boost, he is in the ideal position to capitalize on high-leverage opportunities. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** draws a favorable pairing against Leahy, where wind blowing out adds 10% to his explosive profile. We are also looking for high output from **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Drake Baldwin** (71.83), as both benefit from leadoff or near-leadoff placement, maximizing their chances to accumulate counting stats against the modest pitching of Avila and Houser, respectively.\n\nWhile the core is strong, we are closely monitoring the status of several players. **Gunnar Henderson** (64.32) remains a high-floor start despite a challenging assignment against George Kirby; his dynamic platoon advantage helps offset the tough pitching environment. We are exercising caution with **Sam Antonacci** (55.06) and **Andy Pages** (57.55), both of whom are navigating less-than-ideal platoons against Carlos Rod\u00f3n and McClanahan. The most difficult roster decision today involved **Nasim Nunez** (52.85), who missed the cut by a narrow margin. While **Nasim Nunez** provides elite speed\u2014a priority for this squad\u2014the optimizer favored the higher raw projection of our existing middle infielders over his 9th-hole batting position and the inherent risk of a bench role. We will monitor weather reports closely, particularly for those games involving our hitters in park-boosted environments like the one projected for **Dominic Smith** (62.63) against Houser.",
